Stage: Alpha Status: Draft <p><code>ironroot-client</code> enrolls machines, requests certificates, renews certificates, checks status, and downloads trust bundles.</p> <pre><code>ironroot-client enroll --server http://localhost:8443 --hostname demo.home.arpa --token &lt;token&gt;
ironroot-client request-cert --server http://localhost:8443 --enrollment-id &lt;id&gt; --dns demo.home.arpa --out ./certs
ironroot-client status --server http://localhost:8443 --serial &lt;serial&gt;
</code></pre> <p>For enrollment, <code>--hostname</code> must match the hostname bound to the bootstrap token. If omitted, IronRoot uses the machine's OS hostname.</p> <p><code>request-cert</code> and <code>renew</code> require the <code>enrollment_id</code> returned by <code>enroll</code>. Passing the bootstrap token as <code>--enrollment-id</code> is invalid.</p>
